## Intent & Decisions
The user chose to delete the MCP block instead of changing it to an additive merge. Each machine now adds its servers with `claude mcp add`.

## Actions & Verification
Ran the complete install.sh two times with HOME set to a scratchpad directory that held a .claude.json with one server, a settings.json with a local model key, and a real skills directory. Both runs exited 0. Checksums and mtimes of .claude/settings.json, .claude.json, and .codex/config.toml were identical after the second run. The server, the model key, and the skills directory survived. The installer was not run against the real HOME at this commit.

