## Findings & Constraints
On the machine where this was written, ~/.claude.json held six servers that the old block would have deleted, one of them with a plain-text service token. The user had said earlier that this machine does not want jira or coreweave. Running Claude Code sessions rewrite ~/.claude.json, so an installer that does not touch it also avoids a write race. A machine that wants jira or coreweave keeps its existing entries; a new machine must add them by hand.

